Krun One

This project contains code derived from:

* Laya (Convai Innovations), Apache License 2.0 — DecisionModel, option rendering and build_sequence
  (src/krun_one/model.py, src/krun_one/primitives.py; generalized in src/krun_one/v1/model.py and
  src/krun_one/v1/serialization.py).

Designs adapted without copying code (credited for the ideas):

* GLiNER2 / GLiNER2.5 (Fastino), Apache License 2.0 — runtime label markers scored by a shared MLP,
  label augmentation (shuffle / drop / synthetic names), per-task temperature.
* "Scaling Smart: Accelerating Large Language Model Pre-training with Small Model Initialization"
  (Samragh et al., 2024; HyperCloning) — function-preserving width growth (src/krun_one/v1/growth.py).
* ModernBERT (Answer.AI / LightOn, Apache License 2.0) and mmBERT (JHU CLSP) — encoder architecture, used through
  Hugging Face transformers.

Model weights and tokenizers used for Krun One v1:

* jhu-clsp/mmBERT-small, jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base — MIT (model cards). The tokenizer is the Gemma 2 vocabulary
  (tokenizer.model distributed by google/gemma_pytorch under Apache-2.0); owner decision and analysis in
  docs/KRUN_ONE_V1_TOKENIZER_LICENSE.md (gate cleared 2026-09-26).
* Multimodal towers (referenced, not redistributed in the weights repo): google/siglip2-base-patch16-naflex
  (Apache-2.0), openai/whisper-small (MIT / Apache-2.0), RapidOCR + PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5 mobile ONNX (Apache-2.0).
* Synthetic speech for training data: hexgrad/Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0).

Training data (full registry with revisions: configs/v1/sources.yaml, configs/v11/sources.yaml; audits in docs/):

* Salesforce xLAM function-calling 60k — CC-BY-4.0 metadata; the official card states "This release is for research
  purposes only in support of an academic paper". Used, together with derived sets (MadeAgents/xlam-irrelevance-7.5k,
  nvidia/When2Call), by owner decision (docs/KRUN_XLAM_OFFICIAL_LICENSE_REAUDIT.md).
* CC-BY-4.0: AmazonScience/massive, banking77 (+ c2d-usp/banking77-pt-br, translated with OpenAI models), Taskmaster
  1-3, nvidia/HelpSteer2, ucberkeley-dlab/measuring-hate-speech, MInDS-14, FLEURS, CORD v2, COCO 2017 annotations
  (CC BY 2.0 / no-known-copyright images only).
* Apache-2.0: Team-ACE/ToolACE, NousResearch/hermes-function-calling-v1, gorilla-llm/APIBench (GPT-4-generated
  instructions), Nanbeige/ToolMind (graph_syn subset), OpenAssistant oasst1/oasst2, Johin/function-calling-dataset.
* MIT: multi3woz, MultiWOZ 2.2. CC0-1.0: google/civil_comments.
* CDLA-Sharing-1.0: Bitext customer-support dataset. CDLA-Permissive-1.0: DocLayNet. ODbL-1.0 + DbCL-1.0: CREMA-D.
  CC-BY-SA-4.0: SIB-200 topic labels.
* ODC-By-1.0 (+ Common Crawl terms of use): FineWeb-Edu, FineWeb-2, FineWeb2-HQ, FinePDFs-Edu (continued MLM).
* SWE-bench/SWE-smith (MIT) — v1.1 research only, allowlisted permissively-licensed repositories
  (data/v11/swe_smith_allowlist.json).
* Evaluation only, never trained on: JevBench public items (MIT), BFCL, HWU64, BoolQ, SST-5.
